  "description": "The first-session stall hunt's lab (docs/plans/resilient-mesh/D-hunt.md, section 7.1): 21 dedicated-CPU instances, $1.350 an hour, two billed hours. A mesh in London (the contributor, the source host and a view host on g6-dedicated-4; two forwarders and four edges on g6-dedicated-2) and in Tokyo (two forwarders and one edge on g6-dedicated-2, a view host on g6-dedicated-4: the worst wave 7 instances were far -b distributors); and eight bare g6-dedicated-2 instances that run nothing of Needletail but needletail-nodecheck and the route survey's probes: role `bare`, which the lab tool creates, tags and puts behind the lab firewall like any node and on which the deploy tool installs nothing (its bootstrap gives them chrony). The `hunt` block is the experiment's design (7.2, 7.3, 7.6), read by scripts/linode-stall-hunt.py and scripts/linode-route-survey.py: the arms, the wave 7 control, the nodes with an enlarged hop journal, the echo pairs of the soak rounds, the bare nodes that touch memory, the listeners of each session on the view hosts (7.3: UDP probes, LL-HLS probes over HTTP/3, a needletail-load crowd) and the survey's ends. Sydney is created first and left out if it has no capacity (up --optional-sites sydney).",
